/NOTE: {comments structure}
/ --- [comment] ---   | this is brief decsription of what the next block of code do
/ [comment]           | This is individual line of code comment or more indepth description of what the code block 
/ --------------------------------  | Subroutine separation

/ --- constant used through the program; ---
WHITE,          HEX FFFF
STARTDISP,      HEX 0F00
COUNT256,       DEC 256
THIRTYTWO,      DEC 32
TWELVE,         DEC 12
EIGHT,          DEC 8
FOUR,           DEC 4

ASCII_A,        HEX 041
ASCII_Z,        HEX 05A
ASCII_a,        HEX 061
ASCII_z,        HEX 07A
DELAYCONST,     DEC 1500   


/-----------------------------------------------------------
/ Add your subroutine SubClearDisplay here. (Task 3.1)
/ This subroutine sets F00 to FFF to white
SubClearDisplay,   HEX 0

		    / --- PTR1 = STARTDISP ---
		    Load    STARTDISP
		    Store   PTR1
		
		    / --- COUNT = 256 Pixels ---
		    Load    COUNT256
		    Store   COUNT

CD_Loop,    Load    WHITE                 / *PTR1 = WHITE
		    StoreI  PTR1
		
		    Load    PTR1                  / PTR1 incremented by 1
		    Add     ONE
		    Store   PTR1
		
		    Load    COUNT                 / COUNT decremented by 1 
		    Subt    ONE
		    Store   COUNT
		
		    Load    COUNT                 / if COUNT != 0, loop
		    SkipCond 400                  / skip next if AC == 0
		    Jump    CD_Loop

            JumpI   SubClearDisplay
			
/ --- Variables for the subroutine SubClearDisplay --- 
PTR1,           HEX 0
COUNT,          HEX 0

/-----------------------------------------------------------------
/ Add your subroutine SubInputString here. (Task 3.2)
/ Parameter of SubInputString
InputStringAddr,   HEX 0
SubInputString,    Hex 0 


ReadLoop,       Input                     / read one character from keyboard
			    Store   SI_CHAR           / save character in SI_CHAR
	
		    	/ --- Check if character is uppercase (A to Z) ---
			    Load    SI_CHAR
			    Subt    ASCII_A
			    SkipCond 000              / skip next if char < 'A'
			    Jump    CapHighCheck
			    Jump    StoreDelimiter    / if character < 'A', so not alphabetic therefor it is a delimiter

CapHighCheck,   Load    SI_CHAR
			    Subt    ASCII_Z
			    SkipCond 800              / skip next if char > 'Z'
			    Jump    StoreAlphabet     / in range A to Z
			    Jump    CheckLower        / else maybe lowercase

/ --- Check if character is lowercase (a..z) ---
CheckLower,     Load    SI_CHAR
			    Subt    ASCII_a
			    SkipCond 000              / skip next if char < 'a'
			    Jump    LowerHighCheck
			    Jump    StoreDelimiter    / if char < 'a' and char > Z, so not alphabetic therefor it is a delimiter

LowerHighCheck,	Load    SI_CHAR
				Subt    ASCII_z
				SkipCond 800              / skip next if char > 'z'
				Jump    ConvertToUpper    / valid lowercase
				Jump    StoreDelimiter    / not alphabetic

/ --- Convert lowercase to uppercase ---
ConvertToUpper, Load    SI_CHAR
			    Subt    THIRTYTWO         / ASCII offset between 'a' and 'A'
			    Store   SI_CHAR
			    Jump    StoreAlphabet

/ --- Store the alphabetic character ---
StoreAlphabet,  Load    SI_CHAR
			    StoreI  InputStringAddr   / write character into string
			
			    Load    InputStringAddr
			    Add     ONE               / move pointer forward
			    Store   InputStringAddr
			
			    Jump    ReadLoop          / read next character

/ --- Store delimiter and terminate string ---
StoreDelimiter, Load    SI_CHAR
			    StoreI  InputStringAddr   / store the delimiter
			    JumpI   SubInputString    / return to caller
				
/ --- Variables for the subroutine SubInputString ---    
SI_CHAR,   HEX 0   

/--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ Add your subroutine for painting a character here. (Task 3.3)
/ Parameters of SubPaintChar
PaintCharCharacter, HEX 0
PaintCharDisplay, HEX 0  
/ This subroutine paints a character on the display
SubPaintChar, HEX 0 

            jns SubClearDisplay
		    
		    Load    EIGHT
		    Store   PC_RowCnt             / Set row counter = 8

RowLoop,    Load    FOUR                  / Reset column counter = 4
            Store   PC_ColCnt

ColLoop,    LoadI   PaintCharCharacter    / Copy one pixel from character to print -> display
		    StoreI  PaintCharDisplay
		
		    / --- Advance character pixel ---
		    Load    PaintCharCharacter
		    Add     ONE
		    Store   PaintCharCharacter
		
		    / --- Advance display pixel ---
		    Load    PaintCharDisplay
		    Add     ONE
		    Store   PaintCharDisplay
		
		    / --- Decrement column counter ---
		    Load    PC_ColCnt
		    Subt    ONE
		    Store   PC_ColCnt
		
		    / --- Loop until 4 pixels written ---
		    Load    PC_ColCnt
		    SkipCond 400                  / skip next if 0
		    Jump    ColLoop
		
		    / --- Finished one row of 4 -> skip ahead 12 in display ---
		    Load    PaintCharDisplay
		    Add     TWELVE
		    Store   PaintCharDisplay
		
		    / --- Decrement row counter ---
		    Load    PC_RowCnt
		    Subt    ONE
		    Store   PC_RowCnt
		
		    / --- Loop until 8 rows done ---
		    Load    PC_RowCnt
		    SkipCond 400                  / skip if 0
		    Jump    RowLoop
		
		    JumpI   SubPaintChar

/ --- Variables for the subroutine SubPaintChar ---
PC_RowCnt,    HEX 0                       / number of rows (8)
PC_ColCnt,    HEX 0                       / number of columns (4)


/--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ Add your subroutine for painting a string of characters. (Task 3.4)
StringAddrForPainting, HEX 0
SubPaintString,        HEX 0

/ --- call subroutine SubInputString to get string to be displayed ---
Load StringAddr
Store InputStringAddr
JnS SubInputString

/ --- Iterate for the string to be displayed and take a single character per iteration ---
NextCharLoop,   LoadI StringAddrForPainting
			    Store PS_CHAR
				subt ASCII_A
			    SkipCond 000              / If char < A ->stop
			    Jump CHECKALPHA
				JUMP EndPaintString
CHECKALPHA,     load PS_CHAR
				Subt ASCII_Z
				SkipCond 800              / IF char > Z -> STOP
				JUMP DoChar				
			    Jump EndPaintString

DoChar, JnS SubClearDisplay

	    / --- Compute font address for this character ---
		Load    PS_CHAR
		Subt    ASCII_A                   / get index 0–25; [A = 0, B = 1, ..., Z = 25]
		Store   PS_INDEX
	
	    / --- Multiply index × 32 inline ---
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×2
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×4
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×8
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×16
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    PS_INDEX       / ×32
		store  PS_INDEX
		Load   PS_INDEX
		Add    FontAddr
		Store  PaintCharCharacter         / (Task 3.3 parameter)
	
	    / --- Set display address ---
		Load    Display22                 / Use Display22 to display it in the top left of screen
		Store   PaintCharDisplay
	
	    / --- Paint char using Task 3.3 ---
		JnS     SubPaintChar
	
	    / --- Delay loop (~1 sec visible) ---
		Load    DELAYCONST
		Store   PS_DELAY
		
DelayLoop,  Load    PS_DELAY
		    Subt    ONE
		    Store   PS_DELAY
		    SkipCond 400
		    Jump    DelayLoop

		    / --- Advance pointer -> next char ---
		    Load    StringAddrForPainting
		    Add     ONE
		    Store   StringAddrForPainting
		    Jump    NextCharLoop

EndPaintString, JumpI   SubPaintString

/ --- Variables for the subroutine SubPaintString ---
PS_INDEX,  HEX 0
PS_CHAR,   HEX 0
PS_DELAY,  HEX 0


